# Vendored 9front arm64 per-arch libc — imported as `aarch64`
# (https://github.com/9front/9front @ 350266104f1fed81c78c3d05fa44f523bec0ae4d,
# branch "front", pinned 2026-10-31).
#
# The project's tree name for the architecture is `aarch64` (D-01:
# arm64 == aarch64, the same ISA). Temporary bridge on the way to the
# r9 kernel — see .planning/ROADMAP.md Phase 2.
#
# What was imported: 9front sys/src/libc/arm64/ — the full
# execution-proven ABI/asm set (D-14): 16 assembly files (argv0, atom,
# atomic, atomic64, cycles, fabs, floor, getcallerpc, getfcr, main9,
# main9p, memmove, memset, setjmp, sqrt, tas) + notejmp.c, _seek.c,
# and the mkfile.
#
# NOT imported: the donor's lock.c. 9front modernized Lock to a
# single-word tas spinlock ({ int val; }); Harvey's Lock stays the
# classic { long key; long sem; } with the ainc/adec + semacquire
# protocol, implemented portably in sys/src/libc/port/lock.c — the
# same file that supplies lock/unlock/canlock for amd64 (the amd64
# arch dir likewise carries no lock.c). ainc/adec come from the
# vendored atom.s; the semacquire/semrelease stubs come from the
# 9syscall generator. (D-14 reconcile: drift vs Harvey's libc.h
# surfaced at the first compile.)
#
# Local modifications vs upstream:
#   * mkfile line 1 — objtype=arm64 -> objtype=aarch64 (D-06/D-11
#     rename-on-import) and lock.c dropped from CFILES (above). Every
#     remaining file is byte-identical to the pinned donor except the
#     two reconciles below.
#   * memset.s, memmove.s — the donor reads the n argument with a
#     64-bit MOV, matching 9front's libc.h `usize` (64-bit); Harvey's
#     libc.h declares `ulong` (32-bit) for both functions, so 7c
#     callers store only 32 bits and the donor load picked up garbage
#     in the high half of the slot (a runaway memset loop faulting at
#     USTKTOP was the 02-05 execution gate's first find). Both loads
#     are now MOVWU (32-bit zero-extending), matching Harvey's
#     prototypes. Same D-14 reconcile class as lock.c: 9front's typed
#     size drift, adapted to Harvey's libc.h.
#   * notejmp.c includes <ureg.h> — resolved via /$objtype/include,
#     i.e. aarch64/include/ureg.h (imported by a later plan, post-gate).
#   * main9.s branches to _callmain, defined in the additive import
#     sys/src/libc/9sys/callmain.c (same donor pin).
#
# The 9front typed-atomics declarations (agetl/aswapl/...) are NOT yet
# added to sys/include/libc.h: the asm imports verbatim without header
# dependency and nothing calls the new API yet. The libc.h addition is
# deferred to the phase that has a caller (planner decision, 02-03).
#
# Licenses: MIT-compatible; credit Bell Labs/Lucent, Vita Nuova,
# C H Forsyth, and 9front.
